From 176fc5eeda4eae54fa7b10023c433e1f60beb9cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:08:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Slide videos: upload + automatic big-screen copy (1080p
 H.264) on the server
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Until now a slide video could only be a pasted URL; the server never had the
file, so nothing could be converted. Now:

Editor: "Upload video file…" under Video URL, with upload progress and a live
status ("Optimising for the big screen… 42%" → "Ready · plays a 1920×1080
copy, original 2560×1440 vp9"); a poster frame is filled in automatically.

Server (hanns/video.py, no new table / no migration):
- the slide stores a stable /hanns/video/<id>/ link: it redirects to the
  screen copy when ready and to the original until then (or if conversion
  failed) — slide JSON never changes, so no race with an open editor
- ffprobe decides; a copy is made only when needed (over 1920×1080, not
  H.264 / yuv420p, over 12 Mbit/s, over 60 fps, odd audio, not MP4); light
  files are left alone. Copy: H.264 high, CRF 22, ≤8 Mbit/s, AAC, faststart,
  checked with ffprobe before it is used. Original never touched.
- worker: `manage.py hanns_video_worker` (new compose service), one job at a
  time, nice 15, progress in meta.json; jobs claimed by atomic rename
- no worker running → the upload converts in a background thread; a job
  abandoned by a restart (10 min without progress) is re-queued by the worker
  or by the editor's status check
- Dockerfile installs ffmpeg; without ffmpeg the original simply plays

Tests: real ffmpeg — oversized → copy at the limit + faststart + link
switches; light file untouched; broken file → original plays; worker
command; stale/interrupted jobs; inline fallback; bad ids
